{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>My terror.</b> This is the attribute of justice, in the language of (Exodus 15:16): ״תפל עליהם אימתה ופחד״. And the matter of the hornet (צרעה) is a species of flying creature, such as mosquitoes, hornets, flies, and bees — and they are many species, the general name for all of them being צרעה, just as you find with the plague of locusts in Egypt, which were many species. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that this creature would inject venom into them and blind their eyes and they would die at once, and this hornet went up with Joshua and crossed the Jordan, as written in the book of Joshua. And what is written, three of them and no more — namely ״את החוי ואת הכנעני ואת החתי״ — is because these three were the strongest of all the seven nations and dwelt in fortified strongholds, and He comes to make known a great wonder and a hidden miracle: that with the weakest of all created beings, which is the hornet, the Holy One, blessed be He, would exterminate the strongest of all the peoples in those places."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:24.860517327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}